cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."

title: "Fire Scene Enhancer: Real-Time Image Enhancement for Extreme Fire Scenes"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Edwin Tiong"
    given-names: "Kwong Meng"

repository-code: "https://github.com/MYETKM01/fire-scene-enhancer"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  C++17 implementation of a real-time fire scene image enhancement system
  developed as part of a master's thesis at National Cheng Kung University.
  The system uses fire and smoke masks, dark channel prior dehazing,
  adaptive gamma correction, mask-aware CLAHE, and OpenMP parallelization
  to improve visibility in extreme fire scenes using CPU-based processing.

keywords:
  - fire scene image enhancement
  - computer vision
  - image processing
  - dehazing
  - OpenCV
  - OpenMP
  - C++
  - real-time processing
